/**
 * The `backdrop-filter` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property lets you
 * apply graphical effects such as blurring or color shifting to the area behind an element. Because
 * it applies to everything _behind_ the element, to see the effect the element or its background
 * needs to be transparent or partially transparent.
 *
 * Initial: none. Inherited: no.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Keyword effects:
 * - none: No filter is applied to the backdrop.
